/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 325 0 R
/T (We are excited to announce a new EAAMO initiative led by Juba Ziani and Sanmay Das: Building the Research-to-Practice Pipeline. Longtime members and friends of the EAAMO community, Juba and Sanmay have each spent years working at the intersection of research and practice, leading projects that engage with policymakers, public institutions, industry partners, and communities. Through these experiences, they have encountered many of the opportunities and challenges involved in translating academic insights into real-world impact. This new initiative seeks to build on those experiences by creating a space to better understand, document, and systematize what it takes for research to move beyond publication and into practice.)
/E (We are excited to announce a new EAAMO initiative led by Juba Ziani and Sanmay Das: Building the Research-to-Practice Pipeline. Longtime members and friends of the EAAMO community, Juba and Sanmay have each spent years working at the intersection of research and practice, leading projects that engage with policymakers, public institutions, industry partners, and communities. Through these experiences, they have encountered many of the opportunities and challenges involved in translating academic insights into real-world impact. This new initiative seeks to build on those experiences by creating a space to better understand, document, and systematize what it takes for research to move beyond publication and into practice.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
595 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 325 0 R
/T (The initiative emerges from a central question that has long been at the heart of EAAMO: how can interdisciplinary research contribute meaningfully to addressing real-world problems? While many members of the EAAMO community are actively engaged in applied work, there has been relatively little opportunity to collectively reflect on the processes, partnerships, institutional barriers, and success stories that shape this journey. The seminar series will provide a forum for researchers and practitioners to share lessons learned, discuss effective models of collaboration, and identify recurring challenges in deploying ideas, tools, and evidence in practice.)
/E (The initiative emerges from a central question that has long been at the heart of EAAMO: how can interdisciplinary research contribute meaningfully to addressing real-world problems? While many members of the EAAMO community are actively engaged in applied work, there has been relatively little opportunity to collectively reflect on the processes, partnerships, institutional barriers, and success stories that shape this journey. The seminar series will provide a forum for researchers and practitioners to share lessons learned, discuss effective models of collaboration, and identify recurring challenges in deploying ideas, tools, and evidence in practice.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
596 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 325 0 R
/T (During its first semester, the initiative will operate as a seminar series featuring speakers from across academia, government, industry, and civil society. These conversations will help lay the foundation for a broader community effort focused on strengthening the connections between research, policy, and implementation. Over time, the series is expected to evolve into a full EAAMO working group, creating a sustained venue for collaboration and knowledge-sharing around one of the community's defining goals: ensuring that research not only advances knowledge, but also expands opportunity and contributes to positive social impact.)
/E (During its first semester, the initiative will operate as a seminar series featuring speakers from across academia, government, industry, and civil society. These conversations will help lay the foundation for a broader community effort focused on strengthening the connections between research, policy, and implementation. Over time, the series is expected to evolve into a full EAAMO working group, creating a sustained venue for collaboration and knowledge-sharing around one of the community's defining goals: ensuring that research not only advances knowledge, but also expands opportunity and contributes to positive social impact.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
