/E (A defining feature of the Bridges format was its collaborative ethos. The working groups served as intellectual laboratories where participants could test early ideas, reflect on both challenges and successes, and learn from colleagues working across disciplines and domains. The article captures these exchanges and the insights they generated, while the summaries below highlight the core questions and discussions that animated each group throughout the Fall 2025 semester. Together, these publications serve as a resource for continued learning, ensuring that knowledge generated through our activities remains accessible and can inform future work.)
