681 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 330 0 R
/E (As part of the Spring 2026 EAAMO Colloquium Series, the EAAMO Living Labs initiative hosted a special panel discussion featuring Nadine Krishnamurthy-Spencer \(Chayn\), Marcie Chin \(U.S. Digital Response\), and Monojit Choudhury \(MBZUAI\), moderated by Ashley Khor. The colloquium explored how researchers and practitioners can work together to design, evaluate, and deploy AI systems that serve vulnerable and historically underserved communities. Bringing together perspectives from generative AI, human-computer interaction, public policy, and social impact practice, the discussion examined the opportunities and challenges of developing technology in close partnership with the communities it aims to support.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
682 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 330 0 R
/E (Centered on the theme of "Living Labs with Practitioners," the conversation highlighted participatory and co-experimental approaches to innovation, asking what it means for AI systems to be not only effective but also "safe enough" in real-world settings. Panelists reflected on the complexities of building systems of care, balancing technological capabilities with concerns around trust, accountability, and community needs. The colloquium underscored a core EAAMO principle: that meaningful social impact requires sustained collaboration between researchers, practitioners, and affected communities throughout the design and deployment process.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
