2344 0 obj
<<
/Title (How can responsible AI principles be translated into real-world systems that support vulnerable populations? A recent collaboration between the Living Labs with Practitioners working group and Chayn, a global nonprofit supporting survivors of gender-based violence, offers a compelling set of examples of how AI can be designed, evaluated, and deployed in high-emotion, high-stakes contexts.)
/Dest [30 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2157 0 R
/Next 2527 0 R
>>
endobj
2345 0 obj
<<
/Title (Complementing this work, Safety is a Process, Not a Score, presented at the AAAI 2025 Fall Symposium, introduces a symbol-aware, sociotechnical methodology for evaluating AI safety in social-good applications. The paper describes participatory testing approaches involving survivors and community allies, proposes new ways of assessing safety beyond benchmark scores, and is accompanied by a public Transparency Hub that documents the ongoing evaluation of Survivor AI.)
/Dest [30 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2157 0 R
/Prev 2528 0 R
>>
endobj
